  "description": "Tree One - established apple tree, rear garden - Crown thin by approx. 15%, selectively removing small secondary branches evenly throughout the crown to reduce congestion and allow additional light through the canopy - removal of any dead, damaged, crossing or rubbing branches where appropriate. Intention - retain the tree's existing overall height, spread and natural form. The tree will not be topped or substantially reduced. Reason - To improve the structure of the crown and allow additional natural light into the garden whilst retaining the apple tree as an established feature.",
